Swap-Text 'S-ICD incurs higher 30-year cumulative costs than TV-ICD ($+£1,556$ per patient under Risk $>6\%$; $+£1,823$ under Observed; $+£3,244$ under Risk $>4\%$). Although S-ICD reduces acute implant and lead complications (`1.5%` vs. `4.3%`), the combination of a £2,117 higher device cost per implant/replacement and an 8-year vs. 10-year battery replacement cycle (3 replacements vs. 2 replacements over 30 years) outweighs' 'S-ICD incurs higher 30-year cumulative costs than TV-ICD ($+£764$ per patient under Risk $>6\%$; $+£884$ under Observed; $+£1,602$ under Risk $>4\%$). Although S-ICD reduces acute implant and lead complications (`1.5%` vs. `4.3%`), the combination of a £2,117 higher device cost per implant/replacement and a shorter median battery life (8.5 vs. 10 years, so devices are replaced earlier and more often over 30 years) outweighs'
